## Overview

This change is inspired from [#19478 ](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/19478). 

For bs=1 decode on DGX Spark, the optimal config is nwarps=8 for dense models
- 8 warps x 32 threads = 256 threads per block
- `blocks_per_iter = vdr * nwarps * warp_size / qi`, so the K loop trip count for a row
  halves relative to nwarps=4:
- for small_k narrow rows go with the default generic nwarps

For llama 3.1 8b instruct:
  | Type | vdr | qi | blocks_per_iter @8w | blocks_per_row (K=4096) | iterations 4w -> 8w |
  | ---- | --: | -: | ------------------: | ----------------------: | ------------------: |
  | Q4_0 |   2 |  4 |                 128 |                     128 |            2 -> **1** |
  | Q4_K |   2 | 32 |                  16 |                      16 |            2 -> **1** |
  | Q8_0 |   2 |  8 |                  64 |                     128 |            4 -> **2** |
  | Q6_K |   1 | 32 |                   8 |                      16 |            4 -> **2** |


